  "alignment": "crop both sides to the non-white content bbox, then search a +/-2 px shift and keep the lowest mean difference",
  "comparison_mask": "content mask eroded by 3 px; scenes thinner than that fall back to pixels whose 3x3 neighbourhood is uniform in both images",
  "edge_policy": "antialiased boundary pixels are excluded by design; the reported max_difference can therefore be large on a handful of boundary or singular pixels while p99, mean and outlier fraction are the pass criteria",
  "font_size_px": 100,
  "layout": "6 columns x 320 px cells; COLR v1 glyph via @font-face text at a fixed baseline; SVG via an inline data-URI image with the same viewBox scale; the 45-degree skew scene is captured on its own page because Chrome clips its left overhang inside the grid text layer",
